  "title": "asterix: enum pref variable signedness",
  "description": "It is implementation defined whether a C enum is signed or unsigned.\n(C23 adds a way to specify the underlying type.) The variables that\nwe register with preferences to hold the enum value use ints (not\nthe individual enum types), which is fine and well-defined for anything\nwhere the values fit in an int. It's better to avoid implicitly\nor explicitly changing the sign when using a pointer.\n\nAlso note that packet-asterisk uses int variables (and takes references\nto them), so the struct dialog_cat_struct should also use int instead\nof unsigned.",
  "state": "merged",
